#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:1
msgid ""
"Like FS streams, but with stat on them, and supporting directories and "
"symbolic links, as well as normal files.  Also, you can use this to set "
"the stats on a file, even if you don't change its contents, or to create "
"a symlink, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:6
msgid ""
"So, for example, you can \"write\" a directory, and it'll call `mkdir`.  "
"You can specify a uid and gid, and it'll call `chown`.  You can specify a"
" `mtime` and `atime`, and it'll call `utimes`.  You can call it a symlink"
" and provide a `linkpath` and it'll call `symlink`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:11
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Note that it won't automatically resolve symbolic links.  So, if you call"
" `fstream.Reader('/some/symlink')` then you'll get an object that stats "
"and then ends immediately (since it has no data).  To follow symbolic "
"links, do this: `fstream.Reader({path:'/some/symlink', follow: true })`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:17
msgid ""
"There are various checks to make sure that the bytes emitted are the same"
" as the intended size, if the size is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:20
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:32
msgid ""
"This will create the directories if they're missing, and then write "
"`hello\\n` into the file, chmod it to 0755, and assert that 6 bytes have "
"been written when it's done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:47
msgid "You can pass flags in, if you want to append to a file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:59
msgid ""
"If isSymbolicLink is a function, it'll be called, and if it returns true,"
" then it'll treat it as a symlink.  If it's not a function, then any "
"truish value will make a symlink, or you can set `type: 'SymbolicLink'`, "
"which does the same thing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:64
msgid ""
"Note that the linkpath is relative to the symbolic link location, not the"
" parent dir or cwd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fstream_README.md:73
msgid ""
"This will do like `cp -Rp path/to/dir path/to/other/dir`.  If the other "
"dir exists and isn't a directory, then it'll emit an error.  It'll also "
"set the uid, gid, mode, etc. to be identical.  In this way, it's more "
"like `rsync -a` than simply a copy."
msgstr ""

